# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8-262k window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8-262k and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-1 is the QUAD-FIRST image: built by SB9 from this branch's
# commit WITHOUT the stage-1 evidence (packed_any_evidence_tp4_262144.json and ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.json are PENDING skeletons: the one-card jobs that would
# fill them are DEFERRED). The gate-only 262k profiles carry QWEN_FAST_262K_EVIDENCE_WAIVER=1, which waives both records in a gate run of a gate-only profile and nowhere
# else, logs '262k evidence WAIVED (gate-only)' once, and makes EVERY result of the window UNQUALIFIED (a run, not evidence). No baked default: the eight-seat
# 131k image tp4-serve-8 stays what ships until the owner says otherwise. The node agent is ALREADY stopped (no agentstop, no agentstart, no hand-back in this
# window). Each job names its profile explicitly. A commit that changes a file the image carries needs a new SB9 build and a new tag in every template.
# X0: the first card step of the quad-first window: the status of every board and the all-four reset. The node agent is already stopped and stays stopped:
# there is no agentstop here (the step is broken on the host runner) and no agentstart anywhere in the window. A reset is the only way boards that a
# previous run left hung come back, and links train only at board init. Duration (estimate): 15 min. Stop rule: any failure stops the window.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-1
